nto nut by hand without cross-threading."}}],"manual":[{"n":"1","text":"Print fit_coupon in PLA at 0.2 mm layers, 4 walls, 5 top/bottom layers and 30% infill, without supports. Use identical filament profile and hole compensation for final knob.","parts":["fit_coupon"],"tool":"3D printer"},{"n":"2","text":"Align nut flats with one-dot pocket and press straight in with your thumb until seated. No hammer or pliers. Check recess, invert over a tray and shake gently. If loose, try two dots then three. Select least-tight fit that retains nut and prevents rotation under light hand tightening. For removal, first unthread bolt, then gently push the nut out through the back hole using the bolt tip; do not strike it.","parts":["fit_coupon"],"hardware":["nut","bolt"]},{"n":"3","text":"Default one-dot, two-dot and three-dot interference values are 0.05, 0.15 and 0.25 mm. Set nut_interference to selected value before generating knob. If no socket passes, shift coupon range in 0.10 mm increments and retest instead of forcing the nut. Coupon values always equal nut_interference minus coupon_step, nut_interference, and nut_interference plus coupon_step.","parts":["fit_coupon","knob"]},{"n":"4","text":"Print knob closed-back-down with identical settings. Clear loose strings without filing ribs. Hand-press nut fully onto floor, flats aligned. Verify it is fully recessed and stays captured upside down. Stop if excessive force is needed. No glue or heat is needed.","parts":["knob"],"hardware":["nut"],"tool":"3D printer"},{"n":"5","text":"For a function check, pass M3x16 bolt through closed back and thread through nut so it emerges from open face. In use, hold bolt against rotation and turn knob. This is a captive-nut thumb knob, not a bolt-head driver; it does not lock the nut onto the bolt. Use light finger-tight loads only and keep PLA away from heat. Repeated nut removal can wear the crush ribs.","parts":["knob"],"hardware":["nut","bolt"]}]}
